+
+
+## Plugin configuration layout
+
+- `lua/so/packages.lua`: package URLs managed by `vim.pack`.
+- `lua/so/plugins/init.lua`: explicit configuration load order.
+- `lua/so/plugins/<plugin>.lua`: one settings file per installed plugin.
+- `lua/so/plugins/vimtex.lua`: globals loaded before package activation.
+- Dependency-only or previously unconfigured plugins have documented placeholder files; no new completion engine is enabled by this refactor.
+
+To add a plugin, add its URL to `packages.lua`, create its config module, and add a require to `plugins/init.lua`. Mini's settings moved from `so/mini.lua` to `so/plugins/mini.lua`.
+
+The `ftplugin` directory is removed, including the Markdown pandoc command and buffer-local preview mapping. Existing core options and LSP behavior are otherwise retained for a separate update.
+Marks signs now use `<leader>um`; Gitsigns retains `<leader>ug`.
+
+### Telescope
+
+Existing mappings are preserved except the broken `<leader>fs` snippet picker, now document symbols. New mappings: `<leader>fR` references, `<leader>fc` commands, `<leader>ft` themes, `<leader>/` current buffer, `<leader>fH` hidden/ignored files.
+Normal file search includes dotfiles, respects ignore files, and excludes `.git`. The explicit hidden/ignored search can include dependency folders and may be large.
+Search uses the current working directory; config/package pickers use their dedicated directories.
+Install ripgrep (`rg`) for text search; `fd` is optional. No native extension compilation is needed.
+Within Telescope: Ctrl-j/k navigate, Ctrl-q sends results to quickfix, Ctrl-d/u scroll preview, Ctrl-x/v/t open a split/vsplit/tab, Esc closes. Buffers: Ctrl-x deletes a buffer (Neovim still protects unsaved edits).
+Run `:checkhealth telescope` after applying. No Telescope extensions are required.
